      "writtenOn": "2026-11-06T03:06:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we also clarify how to handle a FRU EEPROM accessed through a USB HID-to-I2C adapter, such as a CP2112?\n\n```\nBMC USB host\n    |\nUSB connector\n    |\nUSB hub (on peripheral board)\n    +-- MCTP USB device\n    |\n    +-- CP2112 (USB HID)\n            |\n           I2C\n            |\n        FRU EEPROM\n```\n\nIn this case, FruDevice discovers the EEPROM on the Linux I2C adapter created by hid-cp2112. Perhaps we could also add a brief explanation of how the I2C adapter maps to the configured Segment and the corresponding USB path and connector.",
      "revId": "dcf96631bd0cd200e457c788221ecf0e41467ff7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e4692e29_5aff5380",
        "filename": "designs/inventory-associations-for-bridged-mctp-endpoints.md",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 446,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002790
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-09T07:06:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One way could be to match the adapter by its parent device, as for an MCTP USB link:\n\n```\n/sys/bus/i2c/devices/i2c-20/device -\u003e .../usb1/1-1/1-1.3/1-1.3:1.0 (hid-cp2112)\n```\n\nThe BMC board alone maps root hub 1 and root port 1 to `USB Port B` and the connector, so the peripheral board can be bound without knowing `i2c-20` in advance:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Type\": \"Bus\",\n  \"Protocol\": \"USB 2.0\",\n  \"Segment\": \"USB Port B\",\n  \"Bus\": \"1\",\n  \"Port\": [1]\n}\n```\n\nThe peripheral board can then describe the CP2112 at hub port 3 below its connector, with an I2C segment holding the FRU EEPROM:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Interfaces\": [\n    { \"Type\": \"Bus\", \"Protocol\": \"I2C\", \"Segment\": \"CP2112 I2C\" }\n  ],\n  \"Name\": \"FRU Bridge\",\n  \"Segment\": \"USB1\",\n  \"Port\": [3],\n  \"Type\": \"USBI2CAdapter\"\n},\n{\n  \"Address\": \"0x50\",\n  \"Segment\": \"CP2112 I2C\",\n  \"Name\": \"Board FRU\",\n  \"Type\": \"EEPROM\"\n}\n```\n\nThis needs FruDevice to record the adapter\u0027s parent device when it reads the FRU, since `i2c-N` numbers can be reused after re-enumeration.",
      "parentUuid": "c5e80d9c_f7d5bf0f",
      "revId": "dcf96631bd0cd200e457c788221ecf0e41467ff7",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
